WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.830 --> 00:00:02.090
Reality warpers.

00:00:02.090 --> 00:00:03.900
Real pieces of work, aren’t they?

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:09.630
It’s one thing when an anomaly is all claws
and fangs, like SCP-682, or if their attack

00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:15.860
of choice is snapping necks like SCP-173,
but it’s an entirely different story if

00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:21.090
an anomaly can turn the air you breathe into
chocolate pudding or shove you into a pocket

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:26.279
dimension that looks almost like our own reality,
except everyone is just a walking, talking

00:00:26.279 --> 00:00:27.279
pile of spiders.

00:00:27.279 --> 00:00:29.019
See what I mean?

00:00:29.019 --> 00:00:30.950
Reality warpers, real handfuls.

00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:35.270
Though, of course, not all reality warpers
are created equal.

00:00:35.270 --> 00:00:40.860
Some are relatively weak, only affecting the
world around them in a mild, ambient fashion.

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:43.850
Others can rattle whole dimensions with their
tremendous power.

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:46.800
The same also goes for morality.

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:53.190
Some reality warpers are loving and benevolent,
such as SCP-343, the kindly, old all-powerful

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:56.020
being known to some as God.

00:00:56.020 --> 00:01:00.410
And some are pure evil beings who want nothing
more than to use their immense power to sow

00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:03.700
chaos and misery among everyone else.

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:08.690
And personally, we can’t think of a better
example of the latter than Bill Cipher from

00:01:08.690 --> 00:01:10.300
Gravity Falls.

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:15.120
This Demonic Dorito wants nothing more than
to take over our dimension and rebuild it

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:17.940
in his image of absolute insanity.

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:25.170
So naturally, we started wondering: If these
two reality-warping titans, SCP-343 and Bill

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:28.400
Cipher, ever came to blows, who would win?

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:32.950
We were so curious, In fact, that we fired
up the Anom-O-Tron 6000, our state-of-the-art

00:01:32.950 --> 00:01:38.409
simulation supercomputer, to see how exactly
the two might meet and how their epic battle

00:01:38.409 --> 00:01:39.540
would play out.

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:42.540
Who do you think would take the coveted W
on this one?

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:47.650
Let us know down in the comments, along with
any other out of universe What If situations

00:01:47.650 --> 00:01:49.070
you’d love to see.

00:01:49.070 --> 00:01:51.860
But in the meantime, let’s fire up the machine.

00:01:51.860 --> 00:01:55.160
Be warned, folks: It’s gonna get weird.

00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:58.650
The date was July 12th, 2013.

00:01:58.650 --> 00:02:02.230
For SCP-343, it had started out as a relatively
normal day.

00:02:02.230 --> 00:02:06.390
He’d spent the night playing solitaire on
the astral plane, before warping back into

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:11.180
his humanoid containment cell by morning,
leaving the Foundation none the wiser.

00:02:11.180 --> 00:02:14.010
After all, he was really here voluntarily.

00:02:14.010 --> 00:02:17.920
If the Foundation had truly wanted to try
to confine him here, they were welcome to

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:22.890
give it a go, but it would be about as effective
as trying to catch a whisper in a butterfly

00:02:22.890 --> 00:02:23.890
net.

00:02:23.890 --> 00:02:28.090
While God had come to this place to experience
the joyful illusion of giving up control,

00:02:28.090 --> 00:02:31.310
it truly was little more than an illusion
to him.

00:02:31.310 --> 00:02:36.530
If he wanted to, he could exterminate the
SCP Foundation in less than an afternoon,

00:02:36.530 --> 00:02:38.720
then retire to Burger King for a Whopper.

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:43.970
So really, they’re all just lucky he’s
a benevolent being, more interested in hanging

00:02:43.970 --> 00:02:48.180
out than dispensing wrath on those he perceived
as insolent.

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:49.900
That was the Old Testament him.

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:52.920
He’d done a lot of soul searching and growth
since then.

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:57.520
It’d been at least a millennium since he’d
smote anyone, for that matter, and the last

00:02:57.520 --> 00:02:59.620
guy really had it coming.

00:02:59.620 --> 00:03:02.620
However, today was going to be a little different.

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:05.640
God knew that something was going to happen
today.

00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:08.739
He sensed a great source of energy emerging.

00:03:08.739 --> 00:03:10.220
Something dark and malevolent.

00:03:10.220 --> 00:03:14.480
He sighed and closed his eyes for a moment,
focusing himself.

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:18.920
He knew, whatever the nature of this threat,
it would fall upon him to face and destroy

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:19.920
it.

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:20.920
How irritating.

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:24.010
He was hoping to finally binge Stranger Things
Season 4 today...

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:27.670
Elsewhere in Site 19, things seemed to be
inordinately peaceful.

00:03:27.670 --> 00:03:32.280
There hadn’t been any containment breaches
or new anomalies brought in.

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:35.430
There hadn’t been any attacks from rival
Groups of Interest.

00:03:35.430 --> 00:03:39.790
Dr. Bright hadn’t even done anything stupid
or started any fires.

00:03:39.790 --> 00:03:43.120
To borrow an old cliché, it was quiet.

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:44.440
Too quiet.

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:49.020
Perhaps the only person who wasn’t having
a relatively mellow day was Security Officer

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:54.400
Frederick Simmons, a mid-level guard who’d
been stationed at Site 19 for four years now.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:57.450
He just wasn’t feeling himself today...

00:03:57.450 --> 00:04:00.710
The work didn’t bother Simmons - emotionally,
at least.

00:04:00.710 --> 00:04:05.050
Typically, even after seeing rather traumatic
things or being in near-death situations while

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:08.599
in containment breaches, it hadn’t left
any lingering effects.

00:04:08.599 --> 00:04:12.770
But lately, he’d been having the strangest
dreams...

00:04:12.770 --> 00:04:14.860
It always played out the same way.

00:04:14.860 --> 00:04:19.329
Shortly after going to sleep, he’d open
his eyes in a strange, multi-colored void,

00:04:19.329 --> 00:04:23.970
surrounded by bizarre, seemingly random floating
objects, none of which seemed to have any

00:04:23.970 --> 00:04:27.050
real relevance to him or his life.

00:04:27.050 --> 00:04:31.750
And just when he’d begin to question it,
the other recurring element of the dream would

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:32.750
occur.

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:37.520
Out of the shimmering, oil-slick rainbow of
mind-boggling colors, a strange being would

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:38.520
suddenly emerge.

00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:46.879
A glowing golden triangle, almost like a drawing
of a pyramid, with a stove pipe hat, a little

00:04:46.879 --> 00:04:53.629
bow tie, thin black arms and legs, and most
notable of all, a single large eye with a

00:04:53.629 --> 00:04:56.809
slit pupil staring out from the center.

00:04:56.809 --> 00:05:00.430
The eye almost seemed to have a strange, hypnotic
quality to it.

00:05:00.430 --> 00:05:03.099
Simmons felt bewitched whenever he looked
into it.

00:05:03.099 --> 00:05:04.099
He wasn’t afraid.

00:05:04.099 --> 00:05:05.930
Quite the opposite, actually.

00:05:05.930 --> 00:05:10.479
For reasons he couldn’t understand, this
strange creature from the world of dreams

00:05:10.479 --> 00:05:12.300
seemed like a good friend of his.

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:14.020
He said, “Well, well, well, well, if it
isn’t my number one guy, the Fredmeister,

00:05:14.020 --> 00:05:15.830
in the house!

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:17.650
I’ve missed you.

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:20.060
Have you missed me?

00:05:20.060 --> 00:05:23.089
Put her there, good buddy!”

00:05:23.089 --> 00:05:25.919
The entity extended his hand, and Simmons
shook it.

00:05:25.919 --> 00:05:31.069
The Foundation guard could feel a strange
tingling sensation jolting down his arm.

00:05:31.069 --> 00:05:36.110
The first time Simmons had encountered the
entity, he’d told him his name: Bill Cipher,

00:05:36.110 --> 00:05:40.819
and he’d told him how incredibly important
it was that Simmons kept their little nighttime

00:05:40.819 --> 00:05:42.249
meetings a secret.

00:05:42.249 --> 00:05:45.469
In exchange, Bill was here to listen.

00:05:45.469 --> 00:05:49.749
Simmons would spend his time in the mindscape
pouring out his worries and frustrations with

00:05:49.749 --> 00:05:53.509
his daily work, as Bill paid impeccable attention.

00:05:53.509 --> 00:05:58.599
The strange little dream entity seemed fascinated
by the work Simmons did - All the peculiar

00:05:58.599 --> 00:06:02.310
and wondrous anomalies he guarded at Site
19.

00:06:02.310 --> 00:06:04.909
But to Simmons, it was all just boring work.

00:06:04.909 --> 00:06:09.240
Zombie-creating supernatural plague doctors
and immortal men with metal limbs lose their

00:06:09.240 --> 00:06:13.740
shine after you see them day in, day out,
for years on end.

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:18.930
Frankly, Simmons needed a day off, but he’d
already used up all his PTO when he’d gotten

00:06:18.930 --> 00:06:20.860
the flu earlier that year.

00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:23.240
He just didn’t know what to do.

00:06:23.240 --> 00:06:25.870
Luckily for him, Bill had a solution.

00:06:25.870 --> 00:06:30.979
Bill, as it turned out, had a fancy little
ability: He could occupy the body of a human

00:06:30.979 --> 00:06:33.559
being, and operate it for them.

00:06:33.559 --> 00:06:37.460
Bill could take the wheel while Simmons took
a load off in the mindscape.

00:06:37.460 --> 00:06:41.839
How hard could standing around, pretending
to look busy at the SCP Foundation really

00:06:41.839 --> 00:06:42.839
be?

00:06:42.839 --> 00:06:46.930
As Bill explained the offer to him, Simmons
couldn’t see any flaws in his reasoning

00:06:46.930 --> 00:06:49.689
- After all, Bill was a friend.

00:06:49.689 --> 00:06:52.219
Why would he have any ill will towards him?

00:06:52.219 --> 00:06:56.999
With that, he shook hands with the bizarre
supernatural triangle, and felt the sudden,

00:06:56.999 --> 00:07:01.559
rough sensation of having his consciousness
ripped free from his body, only for Bill to

00:07:01.559 --> 00:07:03.759
slither in and take his place.

00:07:03.759 --> 00:07:10.009
This new Simmons - The Bill-occupied Simmons
- opened up his demonic, yellow eyes, and

00:07:10.009 --> 00:07:11.009
grinned.

00:07:11.009 --> 00:07:15.610
He gave a demented laugh to Simmons’ floated,
disembodied soul.

00:07:15.610 --> 00:07:21.872
“Oh man,” he said, wiping away a tear
of laughter with Simmons’ finger.

00:07:21.872 --> 00:07:23.210
“That was too easy!

00:07:23.210 --> 00:07:28.639
With your body, I can use the SCP Foundation’s
technology to take over the multiverse!

00:07:28.639 --> 00:07:29.699
See ya, sucker!”

00:07:29.699 --> 00:07:35.419
And with one last demented chuckle, Bill left
for work at the SCP Foundation, with Simmons

00:07:35.419 --> 00:07:39.110
being the latest in his long line of meat
puppets.

00:07:39.110 --> 00:07:43.860
After arriving at Site 19, he sneaked through
the facility, knowing exactly where he needed

00:07:43.860 --> 00:07:44.860
to be.

00:07:44.860 --> 00:07:50.240
You see, Bill is a native entity of the second
dimension - the world of flat shapes - but

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:54.619
he’s able to access the minds of beings
in the third dimension, like us, through the

00:07:54.619 --> 00:07:58.389
medium of the mindscape, rather than the physical
realm.

00:07:58.389 --> 00:08:03.409
Bill’s life goal has always been to find
a way to permeate and take over the third

00:08:03.409 --> 00:08:06.830
dimension, turning it into his personal playground.

00:08:06.830 --> 00:08:11.409
All he needed was the right anomaly to bring
him forth into our world.

00:08:11.409 --> 00:08:18.300
In this case, a little anomalous device favored
by Dr. Kain Pathos Crow: SCP-158, also known

00:08:18.300 --> 00:08:20.190
as The Soul Extractor.

00:08:20.190 --> 00:08:25.169
While Dr. Crow left to the courtyard for his
evening walkies, the being that most people

00:08:25.169 --> 00:08:30.759
assumed was Fred Simmons secreted himself
into SCP-158’s containment chamber and locked

00:08:30.759 --> 00:08:32.120
the door behind him.

00:08:32.120 --> 00:08:37.500
He didn’t have much time; he’d need to
do this perfectly if he wanted a real chance

00:08:37.500 --> 00:08:39.610
at taking over the universe.

00:08:39.610 --> 00:08:42.200
He was amused by the irony, at least.

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:46.210
The fact that, in order to take over, he’d
need to sneak into the midst of the people

00:08:46.210 --> 00:08:48.020
most likely to destroy him.

00:08:48.020 --> 00:08:51.500
Still, where’s the fun in a life with no
risk?

00:08:51.500 --> 00:08:57.520
At SCP-158’s control console, he inputted
the data to soul extraction and set a timer.

00:08:57.520 --> 00:09:01.570
However, there was one difference between
this and the usual procedures performed with

00:09:01.570 --> 00:09:06.200
the Soul Extractor: There was no containment
receptacle on the other end.

00:09:06.200 --> 00:09:09.860
Whatever was extracted would just be released
into the world.

00:09:09.860 --> 00:09:13.010
And this was exactly what Bill was counting
on.

00:09:13.010 --> 00:09:17.900
He laid Simmons’ body down on the gurney
and watched with glee as the robotic arm lowered

00:09:17.900 --> 00:09:18.960
towards him.

00:09:18.960 --> 00:09:25.200
It reached into his chest and pulled out the
essence of one three-sided threat to reality:

00:09:25.200 --> 00:09:26.840
Bill Cipher.

00:09:26.840 --> 00:09:30.670
One quick journey through the bowels of the
machine later, the nightmare scenario had

00:09:30.670 --> 00:09:36.400
come to pass - Bill floated around the room,
dragged into physical reality.

00:09:36.400 --> 00:09:41.340
He let out a long, conceited cackle and spun
his cane around.

00:09:41.340 --> 00:09:43.790
This was going to be fun!

00:09:43.790 --> 00:09:47.290
Elsewhere in the facility, alarms were going
off, and guards were deploying.

00:09:47.290 --> 00:09:52.060
Nobody was meant to be in containment chamber
158, so how was the soul extractor currently

00:09:52.060 --> 00:09:53.060
operating?

00:09:53.060 --> 00:09:55.240
This couldn’t possibly end well...

00:09:55.240 --> 00:09:58.610
Bill, on the other hand, was having a wonderful
time.

00:09:58.610 --> 00:10:02.500
He was pondering all the different ways he
could make the drab, clinical corridors of

00:10:02.500 --> 00:10:06.760
the SCP Foundation into his vision of perfect
weirdness.

00:10:06.760 --> 00:10:11.500
Maybe he’d turn all the researchers into
mice and turn Site 19 into a giant maze to

00:10:11.500 --> 00:10:12.830
run them through.

00:10:12.830 --> 00:10:18.080
Maybe he’d turn the air into farts and release
winged beasts from the hell dimension to ravage

00:10:18.080 --> 00:10:19.080
humanity.

00:10:19.080 --> 00:10:22.150
Maybe he’d go out to the parking lot and
key everyone’s cars.

00:10:22.150 --> 00:10:26.290
Oh, the diabolical possibilities were endless!

00:10:26.290 --> 00:10:31.310
As he floated out into the hall, his fantasizing
was interrupted by a group of Foundation Security

00:10:31.310 --> 00:10:33.730
Operatives wielding assault rifles.

00:10:33.730 --> 00:10:38.420
They entered an attack formation and trained
their rifles on him, before opening fire.

00:10:38.420 --> 00:10:42.220
Bill just found himself laughing again - The
gunfire just tickled!

00:10:42.220 --> 00:10:44.580
“Wow, you guys are hilarious!”

00:10:44.580 --> 00:10:46.560
Bill said between peals of laughter.

00:10:46.560 --> 00:10:51.610
“But wait, I can think of a way to make
you even funnier!”

00:10:51.610 --> 00:10:55.090
He snapped his fingers, and suddenly, the
guards were transformed.

00:10:55.090 --> 00:10:59.810
Instead of the serious first line of defense
for the SCP Foundation, they were now a gang

00:10:59.810 --> 00:11:04.660
of literal clowns straight from the circus,
holding balloon animals molded into the shapes

00:11:04.660 --> 00:11:06.040
of assault rifles.

00:11:06.040 --> 00:11:08.350
They giggled and threw pies at each other.

00:11:08.350 --> 00:11:11.370
Bill was right; this did make them even funnier.

00:11:11.370 --> 00:11:17.670
And he was just getting started, turning this
Foundation snoozefest into a party of cosmic

00:11:17.670 --> 00:11:18.890
proportions!

00:11:18.890 --> 00:11:22.280
Bill began running a rampage of weirdness
across the site.

00:11:22.280 --> 00:11:26.390
Essentially being the ultimate cosmic troll,
he decided he’d simply bother every single

00:11:26.390 --> 00:11:29.260
anomaly he could with his demonic antics.

00:11:29.260 --> 00:11:35.920
First, he appeared in SCP-096’s chamber
and pulled a brown paper bag over his head,

00:11:35.920 --> 00:11:38.960
with the words “UGLINESS LIES WITHIN”
written on the front.

00:11:38.960 --> 00:11:43.900
And just for fun, he then teleported the temperamental
beast to a nearby Amish community.

00:11:43.900 --> 00:11:49.220
It quickly became enraged when a gust of wind
blew the bag off its head, and a man named

00:11:49.220 --> 00:11:51.460
Jedediah saw its face.

00:11:51.460 --> 00:11:55.230
It then killed several others, also named
Jedediah, during the rampage.

00:11:55.230 --> 00:11:57.690
Bill thought it was hilarious.

00:11:57.690 --> 00:12:03.840
He then released SCP-682 into Site 19 and,
just to annoy the creature into further violence,

00:12:03.840 --> 00:12:07.850
he stuck an indestructible party hat on the
monster’s head.

00:12:07.850 --> 00:12:12.540
No matter how hard 682 tried, it couldn’t
remove the party hat.

00:12:12.540 --> 00:12:17.150
This caused it great frustration, which it
took out on any Foundation staff it happened

00:12:17.150 --> 00:12:18.480
to find in the area.

00:12:18.480 --> 00:12:24.060
It had fulfilled Bill’s expectations wonderfully,
but his quest for amusing carnage didn’t

00:12:24.060 --> 00:12:25.060
end there.

00:12:25.060 --> 00:12:30.390
Next, he went to bother SCP-049, the Plague
Doctor, who was in the process of doing surgery

00:12:30.390 --> 00:12:32.900
on a Foundation-provided dead goat.

00:12:32.900 --> 00:12:36.620
With a snap of his fingers, Bill transformed
the Plague Doctor’s surgical tools into

00:12:36.620 --> 00:12:39.120
colorful Play-Doh cutting tools.

00:12:39.120 --> 00:12:42.680
Needless to say, the supernatural surgeon
was less than pleased.

00:12:42.680 --> 00:12:47.590
He was about as annoyed as Dr. Clef was when
Bill turned his favorite shotgun into a bouquet

00:12:47.590 --> 00:12:53.330
of flowers, then sealed his feet into the
floor, or how vexed Dr. Gears was when Bill

00:12:53.330 --> 00:12:59.150
turned his plain beige necktie into a considerably
more loud and colorful tie.

00:12:59.150 --> 00:13:02.480
People there at the time reported hearing
Dr. Gears say, “I just don’t think that

00:13:02.480 --> 00:13:03.480
was necessary.”

00:13:03.480 --> 00:13:08.540
Oh, and he also did some more minor acts of
malice: He filled the break room with an army

00:13:08.540 --> 00:13:13.050
of flesh-eating zombies, he made a moat filled
with molten lava around the site that prevented

00:13:13.050 --> 00:13:18.340
anyone from escaping from his reign of terror,
and he even covered all the walls in cognitohazardous

00:13:18.340 --> 00:13:23.350
doodles that instantly drove any weak-minded
human who saw them into complete, gibbering

00:13:23.350 --> 00:13:24.350
madness.

00:13:24.350 --> 00:13:28.710
It was clear this reality-warping nightmare
needed to be stopped before he got bored of

00:13:28.710 --> 00:13:35.290
playing with his new Foundation toys and decided
to go remodel the universe in his own image.

00:13:35.290 --> 00:13:39.890
Thankfully, there was one anomaly on site
who was up to the task.

00:13:39.890 --> 00:13:44.630
Bill was treating himself to another evil
laugh in the Site 19 canteen when something

00:13:44.630 --> 00:13:45.960
peculiar happened.

00:13:45.960 --> 00:13:51.270
He looked down to see a man in what looked
like a tunic with greying hair and a beard.

00:13:51.270 --> 00:13:55.250
He walked with a peculiar kind of calmness,
his face blank.

00:13:55.250 --> 00:13:57.460
Why wasn’t this guy panicking?

00:13:57.460 --> 00:13:58.810
Was he stupid?

00:13:58.810 --> 00:14:02.230
Bill would seemingly need to teach this guy
a thing or two about fear...

00:14:02.230 --> 00:14:06.400
“Hey, gramps, don’t know if it’s escaped
your attention, but I’ve been giving this

00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:07.940
place an extreme makeover!”

00:14:07.940 --> 00:14:08.940
Bill yelled.

00:14:08.940 --> 00:14:12.410
“Did you forget to put on your glasses this
morning, or are you just that senile?”

00:14:12.410 --> 00:14:14.660
The stranger remained calm as could be.

00:14:14.660 --> 00:14:17.195
He replied with a voice that was measured
as it was deep, “Now, Bill, let’s not

00:14:17.195 --> 00:14:19.010
resort to name calling.

00:14:19.010 --> 00:14:24.230
That’s just childish, don’t you think?”

00:14:24.230 --> 00:14:26.800
Bill’s single eye widened at this.

00:14:26.800 --> 00:14:28.100
“Wait, Wait, hold up.

00:14:28.100 --> 00:14:30.060
How do you know my name?”

00:14:30.060 --> 00:14:31.060
Bill asked, irritated.

00:14:31.060 --> 00:14:34.250
“Are you a friend of the Time Baby or something?”

00:14:34.250 --> 00:14:38.510
He floated over and began circling the stranger,
hoping to intimidate him.

00:14:38.510 --> 00:14:41.320
Much to Bill’s frustration, it didn’t
appear to be working.

00:14:41.320 --> 00:14:47.500
“I know lots of things, Bill, lots of things,”
the stranger replied.

00:14:47.500 --> 00:14:49.570
“That’s my line!”

00:14:49.570 --> 00:14:51.210
Bill screeched, turning red.

00:14:51.210 --> 00:14:53.290
“Who do you think you are?”

00:14:53.290 --> 00:14:56.830
The stranger gave a quiet, reserved chuckle
that infuriated Bill.

00:14:56.830 --> 00:15:01.920
“Oh, personally, I just like to think of
myself as a humble craftsman, watching his

00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:04.870
beautiful creation play out,” he said.

00:15:04.870 --> 00:15:10.560
“But I suppose some of the people around
here like to call me God.”

00:15:10.560 --> 00:15:12.470
Bill didn’t like this.

00:15:12.470 --> 00:15:16.870
This whole universe was going to be his, and
he certainly didn’t appreciate some insolent

00:15:16.870 --> 00:15:20.260
old man acting like he ran the roost around
here.

00:15:20.260 --> 00:15:24.970
Bill would give him an education in who was
really holding the reins - and it would be

00:15:24.970 --> 00:15:29.850
the kind of education that left scars, if
it left anything at all.

00:15:29.850 --> 00:15:34.260
He extended his spindly black arms and released
bolts of lightning against the stranger, who

00:15:34.260 --> 00:15:39.650
simply continued to smile as the electricity
rippled around him, seemingly causing no effect.

00:15:39.650 --> 00:15:41.320
“Are you done?”

00:15:41.320 --> 00:15:42.810
the stranger asked.

00:15:42.810 --> 00:15:45.340
Bill laughed, hoping to hide his irritation.

00:15:45.340 --> 00:15:48.050
“I’m just getting started!”

00:15:48.050 --> 00:15:49.050
He bellowed.

00:15:49.050 --> 00:15:54.360
With a thunderous roar that shook the very
foundations of Site 19, Bill began to grow

00:15:54.360 --> 00:15:55.360
and shift.

00:15:55.360 --> 00:16:01.170
No longer a silly little triangle, he became
a huge, red pyramid of pure nightmares, covered

00:16:01.170 --> 00:16:06.680
in glowing golden arms and teeth, with long,
black tongues drooping out of each level.

00:16:06.680 --> 00:16:12.000
It was the most terrifying and demonic form
in his entire arsenal, and yet, he was astonished

00:16:12.000 --> 00:16:16.300
to find that the stranger still didn’t seem
to show any kind of fear.

00:16:16.300 --> 00:16:20.780
“Very impressive, Bill,” the stranger
said, sounding almost bored.

00:16:20.780 --> 00:16:25.260
“But I think you might be trying a little
too hard.”

00:16:25.260 --> 00:16:29.240
Oh, that does it; Bill would simply have to
destroy him.

00:16:29.240 --> 00:16:31.330
It was a matter of pride now.

00:16:31.330 --> 00:16:35.960
He raised several of his huge, golden fists
and began pounding down on the comparatively

00:16:35.960 --> 00:16:37.660
tiny, humanoid stranger.

00:16:37.660 --> 00:16:41.620
It was an assault so powerful that the ground
began cracking around their feet.

00:16:41.620 --> 00:16:47.050
And yet, it seemed that with almost no effort,
the stranger was able to intercept and block

00:16:47.050 --> 00:16:48.560
every single blow.

00:16:48.560 --> 00:16:50.480
Naturally, Bill was infuriated.

00:16:50.480 --> 00:16:56.029
It was time to finally unleash the full breadth
of his power on this beardy wise guy.

00:16:56.029 --> 00:17:01.570
He launched thunderbolts, fireballs, legions
of giant, mutant wasps, hailstorms, maelstroms,

00:17:01.570 --> 00:17:06.600
bubbles of pure madness, snakes made of barbed
wire, and even incredible coarse language.

00:17:06.600 --> 00:17:12.860
But despite it all, this man - the one who
claimed people call him God - was utterly

00:17:12.860 --> 00:17:13.860
unfazed.

00:17:13.860 --> 00:17:15.860
“You can dish it out,” he said.

00:17:15.860 --> 00:17:19.429
“But let’s see if you can take it.”

00:17:19.429 --> 00:17:20.429
Bill began to laugh.

00:17:20.429 --> 00:17:22.600
“What the heck is that supposed to mean?

00:17:22.600 --> 00:17:23.600
You can’t—“

00:17:23.600 --> 00:17:25.909
God snapped his fingers, and Bill was gone.

00:17:25.909 --> 00:17:26.909
Vanished.

00:17:26.909 --> 00:17:31.130
And with a flick of his wrist, all the damage
and transformations that Bill had performed

00:17:31.130 --> 00:17:32.130
had disappeared.

00:17:32.130 --> 00:17:36.340
It was as though the demonic triangle had
never even been there in the first place.

00:17:36.340 --> 00:17:41.110
Though Dr. Bright, who was acting Site Director
at the time, had some Scranton Reality Anchors

00:17:41.110 --> 00:17:44.269
turned on around the perimeter, just to be
safe.

00:17:44.269 --> 00:17:48.299
You can never be too careful with reality-warping
demons, after all.

00:17:48.299 --> 00:17:52.200
Later that day, Dr. Bright approached God,
and asked him what he’d actually done with

00:17:52.200 --> 00:17:53.200
Bill.

00:17:53.200 --> 00:17:58.159
God chuckled and replied, “For a being of
such immense power, he really had a rather

00:17:58.159 --> 00:18:02.700
childish mindset, so I sealed him away inside
a children’s cartoon, where he couldn’t

00:18:02.700 --> 00:18:04.519
do any further damage.”

00:18:04.519 --> 00:18:06.149
“What was the cartoon?”

00:18:06.149 --> 00:18:07.580
Dr. Bright asked.

00:18:07.580 --> 00:18:12.529
“A charming little Disney show called Gravity
Falls,” God replied.

00:18:12.529 --> 00:18:18.789
Now go check out “Your Questions for God
Answered” and “SCP-096 VS SCP-343” for

00:18:18.789 --> 00:18:21.759
more of this singularly unique reality warper!

